             tilt = low/high shelf pair, dry/wet, no editor; editor files deleted)   ~2 min
  +157  cmake -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release                         38 s (juceaide build included)
  +195  cmake --build --target TapeTilt_AU TapeTilt_VST3 --parallel               141 s, 49 steps, zero errors
  +336  pluginval --strictness-level 5 on the VST3 from the build dir             *** FAILED: Timeout after 30 secs
        -> Gatekeeper alert on Margot's screen: "TapeTilt.vst3 is damaged and can't be opened"
        -> cause: /Applications/pluginval.app carries com.apple.quarantine; loading an ad-hoc-signed bundle
           through a quarantined app stamps the bundle's _CodeSignature with quarantine (0281) and macOS refuses it.
        -> HUMAN STEP #1: Margot clicked Cancel on the alert.
        -> fix: xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/pluginval.app; xattr -cr on both bundles.
  +340  codesign -dv on the built AU: "code object is not signed at all" (JUCE 8.0.9 post-build only ad-hoc signs
        the VST3). Fix: codesign --force --sign - (no --deep) on both bundles; --verify --deep --strict ok.
  +404  AU installed to ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/TapeTilt.component (folder was empty before)
  +407  pluginval --strictness-level 5 VST3 -> SUCCESS                             3 s
  +491  auval -v aufx Tptl Shfv -> AU VALIDATION SUCCEEDED (5 parameters PASS, latency PASS)   1 s
        (auval found the component immediately: the registrar already knew it)

